//
// Served at `/sincero.Simulations/<Rpc>` over Connect, gRPC and gRPC-Web. The reads are
// `NO_SIDE_EFFECTS`, so a Connect client sends them as HTTP `GET`s (cacheable).
//
// The REST routes of docs/api-contract.md, and the RPC that replaces each one:
//
//     POST /api/simulations                      CreateSimulation
//     GET  /api/simulations/{id}[/{path}]        GetSimulation (a `read_mask` replaces `{path}` and `?fields=`)
//     GET  /api/comparisons?ids=…&relative_to=…  GetComparison
//     POST /api/comparisons                      CreateComparison
//     POST /api/simulations/{id}/what-if         CreateWhatIf
//     POST /api/simulations/{id}/cash-ladder     CreateCashLadder
//     GET  /api/fields                           ListFields
//
// Errors are Connect codes (app/controllers/connect_errors.py): `invalid_argument` for a
// `buf.validate` rule (a `google.rpc.BadRequest` detail, one field violation per rule) and for a
// rule of the model, a `SimulationError` (a `google.rpc.ErrorInfo` detail: reason
// `invalid_input`, domain `sincero`, `metadata.index` of the failing item; the model's message
// verbatim); `not_found` for an unknown id.
//
// Partial inputs. The base and candidates of a comparison and the variations of a what-if are
// `SimulationOverrides`: every field optional, each validated when set. What only the merged
// input can break is a rule of the request that merges it (a candidate without `list_price`
// and no `base.list_price`); what only the model knows (FGTS + cash above the list price)
// stays the model's, an `invalid_argument` with an `ErrorInfo`.

